{"name":"Lucky Bamboo","hex":"#93834b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lucky bamboo","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bamboo-like plant, Dracaena sanderiana, believed in some Asian cultures to bring happiness and prosperity to homes where it is grown."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lucky_bamboo"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dracaena sanderiana","blocks":[{"text":"Dracaena sanderiana is a species of flowering plant in the family Asparagaceae, native to Central Africa. It was named after the German–English gardener Henry Frederick Conrad Sander (1847–1920). The plant is commonly marketed as \"lucky bamboo,\" which has become one of its common names, although it is not a species of bamboo."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Dracaena_sanderiana_2.jpg/330px-Dracaena_sanderiana_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dracaena_sanderiana","wikidata":"Q27686509"},{"title":"Bamboo","blocks":[{"text":"Bamboos are a diverse group of mostly evergreen perennial flowering plants making up the subfamily Bambusoideae of the grass family Poaceae. Giant bamboos are the largest members of the grass family, in the case of Dendrocalamus sinicus having individual stalks (culms) reaching a length of 46 meters (151 ft), up to 36 centimeters (14 in) in diameter and a weight of up to 450 kilograms (1,000 lb). It grows in tropical and subtropical regions, especially in Asia. The internodes of bamboos can also be of great length. Kinabaluchloa wrayi has internodes up to 2.5 meters (8 ft) in length, and Arthrostylidium schomburgkii has internodes up to 5 meters (16 ft) in length, exceeded in length only by papyrus. By contrast, the stalks of the tiny bamboo Raddiella vanessiae of the savannas of French Guiana measure only 10–20 millimeters (0.4–0.8 in) in length by about 2 millimeters (0.08 in) in width. The origin of the word \"bamboo\" is uncertain, but it most likely comes from the Dutch or Portuguese language, which originally borrowed it from Malay."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Bamboo_forest.jpg/330px-Bamboo_forest.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bamboo","wikidata":"Q670887"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Donghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG/120px-Donghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Donghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG/250px-Donghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Donghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG/120px-Donghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADonghai_Island_-_P1580772_-_lucky_bamboo.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Dracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg/120px-Dracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Dracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg/250px-Dracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Dracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg/120px-Dracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADracaena_sanderiana_Mast._habit.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Dracaena_braunii.jpg/120